1.  Create a Git Repository
mkdir git-practical
cd git-practical
git init
git status

2: Create a File and Track Changes
cd git-practical
echo &quot;Welcome to Git and GitHub&quot; &gt; message.txt
git status
git add message.txt
git status

3: Commit Changes to the Repository
cd git-practical
echo &quot;First Git commit&quot; &gt; commit-demo.txt
git add commit-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Add first commit demo&quot;
git log --oneline

4: View Commit History
cd git-practical
git log
git log --oneline

5: Undo Changes Using Git Commands
cd git-practical
echo &quot;Original content&quot; &gt; undo-demo.txt
git add undo-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Add original content&quot;

6: Create, Switch, and Delete a Branch
cd git-practical
git branch
git branch feature-demo
git switch feature-demo
git branch
git switch main
git branch -d feature-demo
git branch

7: Resolve a Merge Conflict
cd git-practical
echo &quot;Welcome to Git&quot; &gt; conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Add conflict demo file&quot;

git switch -c feature-conflict
echo &quot;Feature branch content&quot; &gt; conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Update file in feature branch&quot;

git switch main
echo &quot;Main branch content&quot; &gt; conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Update file in main branch&quot;


git merge feature-conflict
If a conflict occurs, edit conflict-demo.txt and remove the conflict markers (&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;, =======,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;). Keep the content you want, then run:
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Resolve merge conflict&quot;
cat conflict-demo.txt
git status

8: Store and Restore Changes Using Git Stash
cd git-practical
echo &quot;Original content&quot; &gt; notes.txt
git add notes.txt
git commit -m &quot;Add original notes&quot;

echo &quot;Temporary work&quot; &gt;&gt; notes.txt
git stash push -m &quot;Save temporary work&quot;
git status
git stash pop
cat notes.txt

9: Configure a Remote Repository
cd /workspaces/git-practical
git remote -v
If origin is not configured, add it:
git remote add origin https://github.com/anandajothi-2007/git-practical.git
git remote -v
If origin already exists, do not add it again.

10: Clone, Push, and Pull Changes
cd /workspaces
git clone https://github.com/anandajothi-2007/git-practical.git
cd git-practical
echo &quot;Push and pull practical&quot; &gt; push-pull-demo.txt
git add push-pull-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Add push pull demo&quot;
git push origin main
git pull origin main
cat push-pull-demo.txt

11: Fork a Repository and Create a Pull Request
git clone https://github.com/anandajothi-2007/Hello-World.git
cd Hello-World
git status

12: Collaborative Editing with Multiple Contributors
cd /workspaces/git-practical
echo &quot;Collaborative editing practical - Exercise 12&quot; &gt; collaboration.txt
git add collaboration.txt
git commit -m &quot;Add collaborative editing exercise&quot;
git push origin main
After the collaborator commits and pushes their contribution, run:
git pull origin main
cat collaboration.txt
git log --oneline -5

